window.docContents[42].resolve({"/Environment-and--___/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment-and--___":{"contents":"The cvc5 types for terms, sorts, solvers, etc. are all related to a notion of (term) manager\nresponsible for allocating and indexing terms and sorts. These types cannot interact and will\nproduce a runtime error if they do not agree on their manager.\n\nThis API abstracts away the term manager completely and enforces manager-consistency statically\nusing a type-class called Ω. Virtually all types in this library have an implicit Ω argument\nthat can be thought of as representing a specific term manager. On the sort type for instance:\n\n#check Srt\n\n\nCvc.Srt [Ω] : Type\n\n\nΩ is an empty Prop type-class and will be erased at runtime; note that you cannot build an\ninstance yourself as the constructor is private.\n\nArgument of the Env monad representing a specific term manager.\n\nΩ is tied to cvc.lean's environment monad Env: Env α, or more precisely @Env Ω α,\ncorresponds to code that uses a specific term manager to produce a value of type α.\n\nThe first problem Ω and Env solve is that manipulating a value v tied to manager m after\nm has been freed is unsafe as freeing m frees v, so v should only live as long as m is\nalive. This is why most features in this library produce an Env _ output.\n\nSecond, as mentioned above, values tied to different managers should never interact as that would\ncause a runtime error. By encoding a specific term manager through an Ω-value, we can type-check\nthat sorts/terms/solvers/etc. are compatible by making sure they agree on their Ω-value.\n\nFor example, the function building an array-sort makes sure the index and element sorts agree on\ntheir manager, and keeps track of the manager associated to the resulting sort by having all of\nthem agree on their Ω.\n\nCreate an array sort.* indexSort The array index sort.* elemSort The array element sort.\n\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API","header":"1. Environment and  Ω","id":"/Environment-and--___/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Environment-and--___"}});